# Keeps `COPY . .` in the Dockerfiles from dragging the host's installed
# node_modules and stale local build output into the build context — those
# are rebuilt fresh inside each image stage instead.
#
# Patterns are matched from the context root with no implicit `**/`: a bare
# `.next` only ever matched a root-level .next, so apps/web/.next — including
# `next dev`'s cache under .next/dev, gigabytes after a few preview runs — was
# sent with every build, copied into the build stage and from there into the
# runtime image (dev-web grew to 6.6 GB).
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
.git
.claude
# The private repo (plans, real-file tests) is never part of an image.
private
